    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests for {@link InternationalFixedChronology} and its associated {@link InternationalFixedDate}. <p> The International Fixed calendar has 13 months of 28 days. Two extra days fall outside the normal week structure and are central to many of the cases below: <ul> <li>Leap Day - day 29 of month 6, present only in leap years. <li>Year Day - day 29 of month 13, present in every year. </ul>"
   },
